$ factory doctor -h
exit 0
--- stdout
usage: factory doctor [flags]

Check that the server is reachable, its version is compatible, the token is
accepted, and the server's own checks: its database is reachable and migrated,
the code host credential works, the sandbox runtime answers, and a cluster
worker is active. With --worker, check this machine as a worker image instead:
git, the agent CLIs and their logins, and the workspace directory.

Each check prints pass, fail or skip, and a failure says how to fix it. Exits 1
when any check fails, after naming every failing check. On a terminal, a failure
with a factory command that fixes it offers to run it.

Flags:
  --harnesses STRING
      with --worker, the agent CLIs to check (default $FACTORY_HARNESSES, else
      claude-code,grok)
  --output FORMAT
      output format: table or json (default table)
  --server URL
      the factory server's URL, such as http://127.0.0.1:8080 (default
      $FACTORY_SERVER)
  --work-dir DIRECTORY
      with --worker, the worker's checkout directory (default
      $FACTORY_WORK_DIR, else $TMPDIR/factory-worker)
  --worker
      check this machine as a worker image instead of checking the server

Environment:
  FACTORY_SERVER       the server's URL when --server is not given
  FACTORY_API_TOKEN    the API token the server was started with
--- stderr
